nds.</li>\n          <li>Build professional System Design habits.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      {Object.entries(TIPS).map(([title, items], idx) => {\n        const id = `c${idx + 1}`;\n        return (\n          <section id=\"id\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">title</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n            <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n              {items.map((t, i) => (<li key={i}>{t}</li>))}\n            </ul>\n            {idx === 2 && <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 \u2014 Architecture tips applied to a canonical high-level system diagram.\" />}\n            {idx === 7 && <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 \u2014 Debugging workflow: sample profile \u2192 trace \u2192 isolate \u2192 fix \u2192 runbook.\" />}\n          </div></section>\n        );\n      })}\n\n      <section id=\"review\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Tips Review</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold\">Top 100 tips</h3>\n        <p>Everything above is roughly ranked by ROI \u2014 start at the top of each chapter and work down.</p>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Productivity checklist</h3>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Timebox decisions.</li>\n          <li>Automate the second occurrence.</li>\n          <li>Prefer async writing to synchronous meetings.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Interview tips sheet</h3>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Clarify \u2192 estimate \u2192 draw \u2192 deepen \u2192 summarise.</li>\n          <li>Every choice justified in one trade-off sentence.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <h3 class=\"mt-3 font-semibold\">Daily engineering checklist</h3>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>One diagram, one decision recorded, one runbook improved.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>How is this different from Best Practices?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Best Practices tell you the ideal rule; Tips & Tricks tell you the shortcut and the reason engineers reach for it.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Should I apply every tip?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No \u2014 treat them as a menu. Adopt the ones that fit your context.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Runbook</strong> \u2014 a written procedure for handling a specific incident.</li>\n          <li><strong>Single-flight</strong> \u2014 a primitive that ensures only one caller does the work while others wait.</li>\n          <li><strong>Feature flag</strong> \u2014 a runtime switch to enable/disable code paths without redeploy.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n          This resource is intended for educational purposes only. Information is compiled from\n          official documentation, academic publications, research papers, industry standards,\n          and trusted educational resources. System Design principles, cloud platforms,\n          distributed systems, and engineering best practices evolve continuously \u2014 readers\n          should consult official documentation for the latest guidance. All trademarks,\n          product names, logos, and intellectual property belong to their respective owners.\n        </p>\n      </div></section>"}